{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nIn `sweep (windows)` diag run 44590213544 (throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl`, the plump-smelly-indianabat fix applied), `tests/unit/test_opcert_service.py::test_completion_pass_spawn_ceiling` (32 git processes, ceiling 30) and `test_completion_fail_spawn_ceiling` (20 processes, ceiling 18) fail. Diffing the job's spawned argv against macOS shows exactly 3 extra steps on Windows. The first is `git show tickets:.bridge_state\\projects.json` where macOS runs `git show tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json`. The other two follow from it: `git add .bridge_state\\projects.json` and `git commit -q --no-verify -m \"chore: seed .bridge_state/projects.json ...\"`. (macOS also runs one `ssh -V` that Windows does not.)\n\n## Cause\n`src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:34` builds `_PROJECTS_REL_PATH = os.path.join(\".bridge_state\", \"projects.json\")`. Line 67 uses it in a git revision path, `tickets:{_PROJECTS_REL_PATH}`. Git tree paths always use `/`, so on Windows the lookup never finds the committed file. `seed_projects_mapping_unit` then rewrites the file and runs `git add` + `git commit` on every ensure sweep. The commit has nothing new to record, so its failure is ignored.\n\n## Approach\nMake `_PROJECTS_REL_PATH` the literal `\".bridge_state/projects.json\"`. Git accepts `/` in pathspecs on Windows for `git add`, so the same constant serves both calls. The filesystem path on line 76 keeps `os.path.join`. No config key, env var or flag. Portable: the change removes a platform-dependent separator from a git object path.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py` — the constant.\n- `tests/unit/test_project_ensures_git_path.py` (new) — the tests below.\n\n## Testing\n- New test (all platforms): `project_ensures._PROJECTS_REL_PATH == \".bridge_state/projects.json\"`, so the git revision path never carries `\\`.\n- New test (all platforms): on a fresh git repo with a `tickets` branch, the first `seed_projects_mapping_unit` call returns `changed` and commits the file. A second call returns `ok`, and `git rev-parse tickets` is unchanged across it, with the file untouched (same mtime).\n- After merge: the two spawn-ceiling tests pass in a `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] On a tracker where `.bridge_state/projects.json` is already committed, `seed_projects_mapping_unit` returns `ok` without writing or committing, and the git revision path it looks up uses `/` on every platform, both proven by tests.\n- [ ] `test_completion_pass_spawn_ceiling` and `test_completion_fail_spawn_ceiling` pass in a `sweep (windows)` run on main."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795113928475737100,"uuid":"27e47209-f5da-4e67-99c9-21b108dec454"}